## 5. Features

### 5.1 Home Screen

The default tab. Shows today's habits and quick access to the weekly view.

**Layout, top to bottom:**
1. Top bar: settings gear (left), "Habit Streak" title (center), trailing space empty (no crown since everything is free)
2. Week calendar strip: 7 day circles showing M/T/W/T/F/S/S with date numbers below; today highlighted in white filled circle
3. "Today" label (or formatted date if a different day is selected)
4. Habit list (scrollable `LazyVStack`): each row shows a circular checkbox on the left, emoji, habit name, and (if streak > 0) flame emoji with streak count on the right
5. Floating action button (+) in bottom-trailing corner opens the habit library
6. Bottom navigation: a custom pill-shaped tab bar with Home and Insights icons

**Interactions:**
- **Tap checkbox**: marks habit complete for selected day. Animate green check with spring scale (0.8 → 1.0), strike through the name, trigger light haptic feedback. If first completion of the day, show toast: "First day of a long streak! Well done!"
- **Tap row body**: opens habit detail (deferred to future; in v1 same as long-press menu)
- **Long-press row**: triggers SwiftUI native `.contextMenu` with Share, Reorder, Edit, Archive, Delete options
- **Tap day circle in week strip**: switches selected day. List re-renders with that day's scheduled habits.
- **Swipe row left**: reveals quick actions (Edit, Delete) via `.swipeActions` modifier (iOS standard)
- **Tap FAB**: presents habit library as a sheet

**Empty state**: When no habits exist, show centered "No habits yet" message with prompt to tap +.

### 5.2 Habit Creation Sheet

Presented as a native `.sheet` with `.presentationDetents([.large])`. Same UI for create and edit (title and CTA label change).

**Fields:**

| Field | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| Name | `TextField`, required. Emoji chip on trailing side opens emoji picker. |
| Frequency | Segmented control: Daily / Weekly / Monthly (custom Picker styled to match the design). |
| Daily controls | 7 circular weekday buttons (S M T W T F S). Selected days white-filled, unselected dark. Above the picker, show comma-separated selected day names. Default: all 7 selected. |
| Weekly controls | Stepper labeled "Nx / week". Range 1 to 7. Default 1. |
| Monthly controls | Stepper labeled "Nx / month". Range 1 to 999 (no practical cap; supports high counts for tracking sub-daily habits monthly). Default 1. |
| Reminder | iOS `Toggle`. When on, reveals a time picker below. Default time: current time rounded to nearest 5 minutes. |

**Footer**: "Create habit" button (or "Save changes" in edit mode) as a full-width white capsule pinned to the bottom.

**Validation:**
- Name must be non-empty
- For Daily mode, at least one weekday must be selected
- Stepper minus button disabled at value 1

**On submit:**
- Create or update the `Habit` model in SwiftData
- If reminder is enabled, schedule a `UNNotificationRequest` for the specified time
- Dismiss sheet and return to home

### 5.3 Habit Library Sheet

Presented when the FAB is tapped. Lets the user pick from pre-built templates or create a fully custom habit.

**Categories** (horizontal scrolling chip selector):
- ⭐ Popular
- 🌿 Health & Nutrition
- 💪 Fitness
- 🧘 Mindfulness
- 🚀 Productivity
- 💰 Finance
- 🚫 Break bad habits

**Search bar** at the top filters templates by name across all categories.

**Per category**: a section header, subheading, and vertical list of habit cards (emoji, name, description). Tapping a card pre-fills the creation sheet with that template's defaults.

**Sticky footer**: "Create a custom habit" white button at the bottom of the sheet (always visible).

**Initial template set** (define in `Templates.swift`):

**Popular**: Gym Workout 🏋️, Drink Enough Water 💧, 7h Sleep 😴, Read a Book 📖, Meditation 🧘, 10k Steps 👣, Eat Healthier 🥦, Social Media Limit 📵

**Productivity**: Plan Your Day 📅, Deep Work 💻, Make Bed 🛏️, Wake Up at Consistent Time ⏰, Prepare for Tomorrow ✍️, No Screen 1h Before Bed 💻

**Break bad habits**: No Junk Food 🍟, Sugar Resist 🍬, Alcohol Free 🚫, No Smoking 🚭, No Snooze ⏰, No Eating Out 🍽️

Add 5 to 8 templates per remaining category. All templates are free.

### 5.4 Insights Screen

The second tab. All time ranges and analytics are completely free.

**Layout, top to bottom:**
1. Top bar: settings gear (left), "Insights" title (center)
2. Time range tabs: **W / M / Y / All** (all four unlocked)
3. Date range label (e.g., "May 11, 2026 to May 17, 2026") with left/right chevron arrows for period navigation
4. Stats grid (two cards side by side): **Completions** count, **Completion Rate** %
5. **Activity Heatmap**: 7×26 grid (rows = days of week, columns = weeks). Cell intensity based on completion count that day. Empty cells dark gray, completions in shades of green. Built as custom SwiftUI view using `LazyVGrid`.
6. **Progress chart**: bar chart showing completion percentage per day in the selected range. Built with `Charts` framework (`BarMark`).
7. **Top Performing Habits**: ranked list showing all habits with rank number, emoji, name, current streak, and completion %. No blur, no paywall. Show as many habits as the user has.

**Calculations:**
- Completions: total habit-completions in the selected range
- Completion Rate: `completions / scheduledHabitDays × 100`
- Heatmap intensity buckets: 0 (none), 1 (1 to 2), 2 (3 to 4), 3 (5+)
- Top Performing: sort habits by completion rate within the range, descending

### 5.5 Context Menu (per habit)

Triggered by long-press on a habit row. Uses SwiftUI's native `.contextMenu` modifier for proper iOS feel including haptics and the system blur background.

**Options:**
- **Share**: presents `ShareLink` with text "I've kept up my [habit name] streak for [N] days!"
- **Reorder**: enters list reorder mode. The list switches to allow drag-to-reorder via `.onMove`. Done button in nav bar exits reorder mode.
- **Edit**: opens the creation sheet pre-filled with the habit's current values
- **Archive**: hides the habit from home but preserves all completion data. Confirmation dialog: "Archive [habit]? You can restore it later from Settings."
- **Delete**: removes the habit and cascades to delete its completions. Confirmation dialog: "Delete [habit]? This cannot be undone."

### 5.6 Settings Screen

Presented as a pushed view from the gear icon.

Sections:
- **Preferences**
  - Week starts on: Sunday / Monday (`Picker`)
  - Notifications: master toggle (links to system settings if denied)
- **Archived habits**: list of archived habits with "Restore" action per row
- **Data**
  - Export data: shares a JSON file via `ShareLink`
  - Reset to demo data: restores the seed dataset
  - Clear all data: wipes the database after confirmation
- **About**
  - Version number
  - Source code link (opens Safari)

### 5.7 Notifications

For habits with `reminderEnabled == true`:
- Schedule a daily `UNCalendarNotificationTrigger` at the specified hour/minute
- Notification title: habit name + emoji
- Notification body: "Time for your daily habit. Keep the streak going!"
- Request notification authorization on first reminder enabled

If user denies notification permission, show a one-time alert explaining the feature won't work and offer a deep link to Settings.

